# `yo fix --migrate deref` inserts `.*` where a reference is read as a whole
# value of a `Copy` type (b.yo: `take_i(r.*)`), and where a move-only referent
# is only read (d.yo: the operands of `r.* == o.*`). Where the evaluation
# copies a move-only referent, `r.*` would be E0901, so that `String` site
# (a.yo: a by-value argument) is listed and left as written
# (issues/fixed/2026-11-05-migrate-deref-copies-a-move-only-referent-into-a-by-value-parameter.md).
# c.yo's `x := r` is NOT a site: a reference-binding read is a reference leaf,
# so the `:=` binds the reference and copies nothing (VERDICTS-41 R-TAIL,
# VERDICTS-23 R1; tests/local_borrows.test.yo `_bind_ref_whole`). c.yo
# evaluates, is not listed and keeps its text.
# One site per file: a file whose evaluation stops (at the E0901 the kept copy
# still raises) is migrated only up to that point. That makes `fix` exit 1,
# and the harness stops a case at its first non-zero command, so no command
# can follow it here.
stdout_keep=^(fix:|error|help)
timeout=240
